# "YAML header" plugin

I would you like to generate a plan for a new plugin (in the grammars
directory). You will look at the corresponding skill for writting plugins.

The plugins will contain a ANTLR grammar for extracting a YAML header at the
begining of a file : ie. lines of comma-searated field/value pairs, wrapped
between two lines of triple dashes. All other lines in the text are ignored.

You will create a class TextHeader that extends CorpusObject, and contains a list
of pairs key/values from the YAML header.

You will create a class TextHeaderViewFactory that implements
ObjectViewFactory<TextHeader>

TextHeaderViewFactory will be registerd as a service in
resources/META-INF/services/fr.cnrs.lacito.matchbox.grammarfx.ObjectViewFactory

The text header view factory will contains a two columns table: a column for
the field name, and a column for the field value, and as many rows as there are
fields in the header.

The table will be editable, so the user can modify the field values: if the user
modifying a value in a cell and hit enter, the underlying corpus object will be
updated, and the content of the file at the given coordinates is updated. If he
or she hit escape, the cell value is reverted to its original value.

# "Media reference" plugin

You will create a plan for a plugin for reference to audio pages.

You will look at the corresponding skill for writting plugins.

An "media reference" is a one-line convention that indicates the start or end of
media segment (audio and video). A media segment is a portion of a media file
(audio or video).

It has two forms: either it gives a file name, plus a start and end offsets in
milliseconds, or it gives only a start and end time offset in milliseconds but
no filename, and the filename is extracted from the text header. The file name
can be relative (to the file parsed) or absolute (to the root of the file
system).

Which convention would you suggest for writing audio markers?

You will create a class MediaMarker that extends CorpusObject, and contains a resolved path to the media file, and the start and end offsets in milliseconds.

You will create a class MediaMarkerViewFactory that implements ObjectViewFactory<MediaMarker>.

MediaMarkerViewFactory will be registerd as a service in
resources/META-INF/services/fr.cnrs.lacito.matchbox.grammarfx.ObjectViewFactory

The media marker view factory will contains a player for a sound file or a video file, using javafx media capabilities.

In order to avoid reopening the file for each different media marker, a single
player instance will be shared by all media marker views, and/or each media file
refered to in the text file will be opened only once. Maybe, in order to achieve
that, it will be necessary to use the TextHeader object: add method to the
textheader object for accessing the list of all media files referenced in the text.

# lift-patchbox view

I would you like to generate a plan for a new plugin (in the grammars
directory). You will look at the corresponding skill for writting plugins.

The plugins will recognize and parse LiftPatchShort syntax, i.e. a syntax for
expressing lexical information. a library containing a parser for this language
is in the ../lift-patchbox directory. Please report if you cannot access it.

